---
layout: layouts/base.njk
description: >-
  Nadia Sultan Rana builds the models and the checks that decide whether a
  number can be trusted. Data modeling, reconciliation, data quality and
  structured evaluation.
---
{% from "macros/components.njk" import EditorialHeading, RecordMetadata, EditorialIndex, Marker, QuietEmptyState %}

{# ===================================================================
   Hero. Her name, what she does, and one photograph.
   =================================================================== #}
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="name-h">
  <p class="hero__kicker">{{ site.author.role }} · M.S. candidate, Northeastern</p>
  <h1 class="hero__name" id="name-h">{{ site.title }}</h1>
  <p class="hero__lead">I build the models and the checks that decide whether
    a number can be trusted.</p>
  <p class="hero__links">
    <a href="mailto:{{ site.author.email }}">{{ site.author.email }}</a>
    <a href="/#work">See the work</a>
  </p>

  <div class="hero__figure">
    {% mediaFigure
       "hero-canyon.jpg",
       "Nadia Sultan Rana standing between two sandstone walls in a narrow canyon, back to the camera, one hand resting on the rock either side.",
       "Sandstone, worked into shape by water over a longer run than anybody was watching for.",
       "Photograph · 2024",
       "(min-width: 1536px) 1184px, (min-width: 1200px) calc(100vw - 256px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 128px), calc(100vw - 48px)",
       "eager" %}
  </div>
</section>

{# =================================================================== #}
<section class="section" id="approach" aria-labelledby="approach-h">
  {{ EditorialHeading(
    "What I do",
    "Most of my work is making two systems agree on what a record means.",
    "Data models and dictionaries that hold up when somebody else uses them, reconciliation between systems that were never built to match, validation rules that catch the records worth a second look, and evaluation scored against written criteria rather than impressions.",
    "h2", "approach-h") }}

  <div class="prose section__body">
    <p>Currently a master&rsquo;s candidate in data analytics engineering at
      Northeastern, looking for full-time analytics roles.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{# ===================================================================
   Work. Five entries, one fixed shape.

   Every entry fills every slot: role, dates, tools, and exactly one
   headline figure. The schema lives in src/_data/work.js so it cannot
   drift entry to entry, which is what made the previous version read
   as unfinished. See DESIGN_SYSTEM.md, RecordMetadata / Schema A.
   =================================================================== #}
<section class="section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-h">
  {{ EditorialHeading(
    "Five roles · 2023 – 2026",
    "Work",
    "Each entry states the role, the place, the dates, the tools, and one figure it can stand behind.",
    "h2", "work-h") }}

  <ol class="numbered">
    {%- for job in work %}
    <li>
      <article class="entry__grid" aria-labelledby="job-{{ loop.index }}">
        <p class="entry__numeral" aria-hidden="true">{{ loop.index | pad }}</p>

        <div class="entry__main">
          <h3 class="entry__org" id="job-{{ loop.index }}">{{ job.org }}</h3>
          <div class="entry__body">
            {%- for para in job.body %}
            <p>{{ para | safe }}</p>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>
          {{ Marker(job.marker) }}
        </div>

        <div class="entry__side">
          {{ RecordMetadata([
            { label: "Role",  value: job.role },
            { label: "Place", value: job.place },
            { label: "Dates", value: job.dates }
          ], job.org + " record") }}

          <p class="evidence">
            <span class="evidence__value">{{ job.evidence.value }}</span>
            <span class="evidence__label">{{ job.evidence.label }}</span>
          </p>

          <ul class="tools">
            {%- for tool in job.tools %}<li>{{ tool }}</li>{% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

{# ===================================================================
   The project. One entry, and it is not padded out to look like more.
   =================================================================== #}
<section class="section" id="project" aria-labelledby="project-h">
  {{ EditorialHeading(
    "Case study",
    "Project",
    "One finished study, with the method and the limitations published next to the finding.",
    "h2", "project-h") }}

  {%- set items = [] %}
  {%- for p in collections.projects %}
  {%- set items = (items.push({
    index: loop.index | pad,
    title: p.data.title,
    href: p.url,
    summary: p.data.description,
    meta: p.data.period
  }), items) %}
  {%- endfor %}

  {%- if items.length %}
  {{ EditorialIndex(items, "Projects") }}
  {%- else %}
  {{ QuietEmptyState() }}
  {%- endif %}
</section>

{# =================================================================== #}
<section class="section" id="now" aria-labelledby="now-h">
  {{ EditorialHeading(
    "September 2026",
    "Now",
    "Kept short, because a stale “now” is worse than none.",
    "h2", "now-h") }}

  <div class="section__body">
    {{ RecordMetadata([
      { label: "Studying",    value: "M.S. Data Analytics Engineering, Northeastern. 2026–2027." },
      { label: "Looking for", value: "Full-time analytics roles." }
    ], "Current status") }}
  </div>
</section>

{# =================================================================== #}
<section class="section" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-h">
  {{ EditorialHeading(
    "Get in touch",
    "Contact",
    "Email is the reliable route.",
    "h2", "contact-h") }}

  <ul class="contact__list section__body">
    <li><a href="mailto:{{ site.author.email }}">{{ site.author.email }}</a></li>
    <li><a href="{{ site.author.linkedin }}" rel="me">linkedin.com/in/nadiasrana</a></li>
    <li>{{ site.author.location }}</li>
  </ul>

  {{ Marker("[BLOCKED: the résumé PDF is in the repo and confirmed text-based, but the link is not wired and the file is not published. It carries six items CONTENT.md blocks or has corrected — including a superseded pair of R² figures that the project page exists to correct. They are listed in CONTENT.md under Résumé PDF; they are deliberately not repeated here, because a marker that quotes a blocked figure publishes it. Supply a cleaned PDF, then set site.resume.cleared = true.]") }}

</section>
